\section{Discussion}

In this work we have introduced a simple auxiliary loss that encourages the distribution of activations in a deep network towards a standardized Gaussian. We find that adding this secondary objective accelerates the training by almost 2-fold on the primary classification objective for a range of network architectures, and the resulting network can be trained across a wide range of batch sizes.

